{
  "version": 2,
  "notes": [
    "Which skill has to be held before another can be taught.",
    "Ids are '<subject_id>:<topic_id>', the same ids the attempt log and the",
    "mastery roll-up use. The Branch Decision Engine reads this: a child who",
    "answers wrong while the weakest prerequisite here sits below 0.40 is",
    "taken back to that prerequisite for a short micro-lesson instead of",
    "being re-explained the thing they were never ready for.",
    "",
    "Two authoring rules, both of which the file keeps:",
    "1. Only chains where the skill genuinely grows - counting bands, the",
    "   Hindi vowel and consonant order, letters before words before",
    "   reading. Letters of the alphabet are NOT chained to each other: not",
    "   knowing C does not make B unteachable.",
    "2. A prerequisite must be a topic that can actually gain mastery. A",
    "   topic whose activities are all watch-and-trace never produces a",
    "   graded attempt, so an edge to it would send a child backwards for",
    "   ever. Those edges are left out on purpose.",
    "",
    "The loader validates this at startup: ids must parse, no self",
    "references, no cycles."
  ],
